cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "Phydroperiod: hydroperiod from water mask time series"
abstract: >-
  Python library that computes hydroperiod — the number of days a pixel holds
  water over a hydrological cycle — from a time series of water masks. It
  implements the midpoint weighting scheme of J. Bustamante, in which each scene
  is weighted by the stretch of the cycle it stands for rather than counted as a
  single observation, and adds per-pixel tracking of valid observations, so that
  a partly cloudy scene contributes wherever it is clear. From that it derives
  the first and last flood day, a temporal representativity index per pixel and
  for the collection, and the hydroperiod normalised to a 365-day cycle. It
  needs only the masks and a cycle start, with nothing particular to a site.
type: software
